-- g8-fees-as-made.l4: the Fees Regulations as made (Kovetz HaTakanot 11951, p. 2116, 9 July 2025), regulations 1 to 5.
--
-- THE TEXT QUOTED HERE.  The gazette's text layer is bidirectionally scrambled and carries the margin headings
-- inside its lines, so the quotations below are the CONSOLIDATED wiki's lines (inputs/regulations-fees.wiki, cited
-- as src:fees:N) for every provision that the 2026 amendment did not touch, and the gazette's own lines
-- (inputs/kovetz-hatakanot-11951-p2116.txt, cited as src:kt11951:N, direction marks replaced by spaces) for regulation 2(b),
-- the one provision where the text as made differs from the consolidated text.  That the words of regulations
-- 1(def), 2(a), 2(c), 2(d), 3, 4 and 5 are, word for word, the words the gazette printed was checked by script
-- (work/g8/cmp_asmade.py: the only words in the gazette that the wiki lacks are margin headings and letters of
-- sub-regulations; the only words in the wiki that the gazette lacks are in 2(b)) and against the page image of p. 2116.
-- The wiki's "(adjusted to 2025)" notes are the wiki editor's: the gazette prints no such note (page image).
-- Figures were read from the page image: 194, 40, 284, 398.
--
-- THE VINTAGE IS AN INPUT.  This module answers for the text as made only; it never reads the draft or the
-- amendment.  A service this text does not price answers NOTHING.

§ `The Fees Regulations as made (Kovetz HaTakanot 11951, 9 July 2025)`

§§ `The preamble (inert: it names the empowering sections and two approvals)`

-- src:fees:10 | בתוקף סמכותי לפי {{ח:חיצוני|חוק הסדרת העיסוק בעבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר#סעיף 59|סעיפים 59}} {{ח:חיצוני|חוק הסדרת העיסוק בעבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר#סעיף 60|ו־60}} {{ח:חיצוני|חוק הסדרת העיסוק בעבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר|לחוק הסדרת העיסוק בעבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר, התשפ״ה–2025}} (להלן – החוק), באישור שר האוצר לפי {{ח:חיצוני|חוק יסודות התקציב#סעיף 39ב|סעיף 39ב לחוק יסודות התקציב, התשמ״ה–1985}}, ובאישור ועדת העבודה והרווחה של הכנסת, אני מתקין תקנות אלה:
-- Paraphrase (mine; the Hebrew governs): in exercise of my powers under sections 59 and 60 of the Law
-- (the Law: the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or Air-Conditioning Systems Law 5785-2025),
-- with the approval of the Minister of Finance under section 39B of the Budget Principles Law 5745-1985 and the
-- approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee, I make these regulations.
-- Nothing computes from the two approvals; the encoding carries the empowering sections as data.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, preamble (src:fees:10)
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the sections of the Law under which the Fees Regulations are made` MEANS
    LIST 59, 60

§§ `Regulation 5: commencement`

-- Kind C, a commencement counted from another date.  IL s.10(c) is NOT applied (the brief's ruling 4); the
-- alternatives below are callable.  The gazette issue is dated 9 July 2025 (a Wednesday).
-- src:kt11951:12 | קובץ התקנות,11951 י"ג בתמוז התשפ"ה 9.7.2025,
-- src:fees:41 | {{ח:ת}} תחילתן של תקנות אלה 7 ימים מיום פרסומן {{ח:הערה|(התקנות פורסמו ביום 9.7.2025, ותחילתן ביום 16.7.2025)}}.
-- Paraphrase (mine): the commencement of these regulations is 7 days from the day of their publication.
-- The wiki's note says: published 9.7.2025, commencing 16.7.2025.  IL s.10(a): a period of days "from" a day does
-- not count that day, so the last day of the 7 days is 16.7.2025, and that is the commencement day taken here.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 5 (src:fees:41); the gazette issue date (src:kt11951:12)
GIVETH A DATE
`the Fees Regulations as made were published on` MEANS
    YMD 2025 7 9

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 5 (src:fees:41); Interpretation Law s 10(a)
GIVETH A DATE
`the Fees Regulations as made came into force on` MEANS
    `s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 7 `days from` `the Fees Regulations as made were published on`

-- Alternative 1 (fork on kind C): the commencement is the day AFTER the 7 days have run, 17.7.2025.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 5 (src:fees:41); Interpretation Law s 10(a)
GIVETH A DATE
`the Fees Regulations as made came into force on, taking the day after the seven days have run` MEANS
    `s 10 — the first day of a period counted from or after an event on` `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on`

-- Alternative 2 (fork on IL s.10(c) for kind C): the last day moves while it is a day of rest, recess or holiday.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 5 (src:fees:41); Interpretation Law s 10(a), (c)
GIVEN calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days`
GIVETH A DATE
`the Fees Regulations as made came into force on, applying IL s 10(c) under` calendar MEANS
    `s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 7 `days from` `the Fees Regulations as made were published on` `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (calendar's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))

-- The moment, by Interpretation Law s 21: 00:01 on the commencement day.  Regulation 5 is the "other provision"
-- of Law s 1 as to the DAY; it names no moment, so the Law's default moment applies.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 5 (src:fees:41); Interpretation Law s 21
GIVETH A Moment
`the Fees Regulations as made begin to bind at` MEANS
    `s 21 — the moment a statute begins to bind, commencing on` `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on`

§§ `Regulation 1: definition`

-- src:fees:17 | {{ח:ת}} בתקנות אלה,
-- src:fees:18 | {{ח:ת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”בחינה מעשית“ – בחינה להערכת הידע והמיומנויות המעשיות של לומד בקורס הכשרה מקצועית המופיעים בתוכנית הלימודים לעניין התקנה ושירות למיתקני קירור ומיזוג אוויר;
-- Paraphrase (mine): in these regulations, "practical exam" means an exam to assess the practical knowledge and
-- skills of a learner in a vocational training course that appear in the curriculum for the installation and
-- service of refrigeration and air-conditioning facilities.
-- Regulation 1 as made defines ONE term.  The wiki's heading note reads the singular heading as a slip for the
-- plural; as made there was one definition, and the singular was exact.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 1, "practical exam" (src:fees:17-18)
GIVEN exam IS AN `Exam in a vocational training course`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`as made, regulation 1 — the exam is a practical exam` exam MEANS
        exam's `assesses the practical knowledge and skills of the learner`
    ... exam's `taken by a learner in a vocational training course`
    ... exam's `on subjects in the curriculum for the installation and service of cooling facilities`

-- The text as made defines no "theoretical exam" and uses none.  A definition the text does not give is not
-- FALSE: it is a named refusal, returned and never stored.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Fees Regulations as made define no theoretical exam` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Fees Regulations as made define no theoretical exam"

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 1 (src:fees:17-18)
GIVEN exam IS AN `Exam in a vocational training course`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`as made, regulation 1 — the exam is a theoretical exam` exam MEANS
    `the Fees Regulations as made define no theoretical exam`

§§ `Regulation 2: fees`

-- The figures are those of the gazette page image (194, 40, 284, 398).  Each figure took effect on the commencement
-- day of these regulations, and that is the day regulation 3 counts its update days from.

-- src:fees:24 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} בעד בחינה מעשית, ישלם הנבחן אגרה בסכום של 194 שקלים חדשים {{ח:הערה|(מתואם לשנת 2025)}}.
-- Paraphrase (mine): for a practical exam, the examinee shall pay a fee of NIS 194.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 2(a) (src:fees:24)
GIVETH A `Fee stated in a vintage`
`as made, regulation 2(a) — the fee for a practical exam` MEANS
    `Fee stated in a vintage` WITH
        `the amount stated` IS 194
        `the provision that states it` IS "2(a)"
        `the payer the provision names` IS JUST `the examinee under the Fees Regulations`
        `the day the stated amount took effect` IS JUST `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on`
        `an objection charge rather than a fee` IS FALSE

-- src:kt11951:26 | (ב) הוגשה השגה על ציון הבחינה, ישלם מגיש ההשגה, נוסף על התשלום בעד
-- src:kt11951:27 | האגרה כאמור בתקנת משנה (א), סכום של 40 שקלים חדשים, בעד כל השגה.
-- Paraphrase (mine): where an objection is lodged to the score of THE exam, the person who lodges it shall pay,
-- in addition to the payment of the fee as stated in sub-regulation (a), NIS 40 for each objection.
-- "The exam" is not defined: the one exam the regulations define is the practical exam, and (a) is its fee.
-- Whether the objection charge is the whole of what the objector pays or comes on top of a fresh exam fee, and
-- whether "the exam" reaches the theoretical exam, are forks (FRAGMENT-G8.md); both have callable readings.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 2(b) (src:kt11951:26-27)
GIVETH A `Fee stated in a vintage`
`as made, regulation 2(b) — the charge for an objection to the score of the exam` MEANS
    `Fee stated in a vintage` WITH
        `the amount stated` IS 40
        `the provision that states it` IS "2(b)"
        `the payer the provision names` IS JUST `the objector under the Fees Regulations`
        `the day the stated amount took effect` IS JUST `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on`
        `an objection charge rather than a fee` IS TRUE

-- src:fees:27 | {{ח:תת|(ג)}} בעד קבלת רישיון או חידושו לפי {{ח:חיצוני|חוק הסדרת העיסוק בעבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר#סעיף 5|סעיף 5 לחוק}}, ישלם מבקש הרישיון אגרה בסכום של 284 שקלים חדשים {{ח:הערה|(מתואם לשנת 2025)}}.
-- Paraphrase (mine): for receiving a licence or renewing it under section 5 of the Law, the applicant for the
-- licence shall pay a fee of NIS 284.  The fee is on the RECEIPT of the licence, where the draft priced the
-- APPLICATION; and the section cited is section 5, which is the section on applying (fork and contradiction note).
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 2(c) (src:fees:27)
GIVETH A `Fee stated in a vintage`
`as made, regulation 2(c) — the fee for receiving a licence or renewing it` MEANS
    `Fee stated in a vintage` WITH
        `the amount stated` IS 284
        `the provision that states it` IS "2(c)"
        `the payer the provision names` IS JUST `the licence applicant under the Fees Regulations`
        `the day the stated amount took effect` IS JUST `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on`
        `an objection charge rather than a fee` IS FALSE

-- src:fees:28 | {{ח:תת|(ד)}} בעד בקשה לקבלת רישיון זמני למומחה זר או לחידושו לפי {{ח:חיצוני|חוק הסדרת העיסוק בעבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר#סעיף 9|סעיף 9 לחוק}}, ישלם מבקש הרישיון אגרה בסכום של 398 שקלים חדשים {{ח:הערה|(מתואם לשנת 2025)}}.
-- Paraphrase (mine): for an application to receive a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or to renew it,
-- under section 9 of the Law, the applicant for the licence shall pay a fee of NIS 398.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 2(d) (src:fees:28)
GIVETH A `Fee stated in a vintage`
`as made, regulation 2(d) — the fee for an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal` MEANS
    `Fee stated in a vintage` WITH
        `the amount stated` IS 398
        `the provision that states it` IS "2(d)"
        `the payer the provision names` IS JUST `the licence applicant under the Fees Regulations`
        `the day the stated amount took effect` IS JUST `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on`
        `an objection charge rather than a fee` IS FALSE

-- What the text as made states for each head of section 59.  A head it does not price answers NOTHING.
-- The reading of "the exam" in 2(b) is a parameter; the taken reading is the one defined exam, the practical exam.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 2(a) to (d); Law s.59
GIVEN reading IS A `Reading of "the exam" in regulation 2(b) as made`
      service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Fee stated in a vintage`
`the Fees Regulations as made state, reading "the exam" in regulation 2(b) as` reading `, for the service` service MEANS
    CONSIDER service
    WHEN `the service of filing an application for a licence or its renewal` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal`
        THEN JUST `as made, regulation 2(c) — the fee for receiving a licence or renewing it`
    WHEN `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal`
        THEN JUST `as made, regulation 2(d) — the fee for an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal`
    WHEN `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the service of sitting a practical exam`
        THEN JUST `as made, regulation 2(a) — the fee for a practical exam`
    WHEN `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam`
        THEN JUST `as made, regulation 2(b) — the charge for an objection to the score of the exam`
    WHEN `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam`
        THEN CONSIDER reading
             WHEN `the exam is the one exam the regulations define` THEN NOTHING
             WHEN `the exam is any exam`
                 THEN JUST `as made, regulation 2(b) — the charge for an objection to the score of the exam`
    WHEN `the service of attending a continuing training course` THEN NOTHING

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 2(a) to (d); Law s.59
GIVEN service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Fee stated in a vintage`
`the Fees Regulations as made state, for the service` service MEANS
    `the Fees Regulations as made state, reading "the exam" in regulation 2(b) as` `the exam is the one exam the regulations define` `, for the service` service

-- Alternative for the first contradiction noted in FRAGMENT-G8.md: regulation 2(c) speaks of "receiving a licence or
-- renewing it under section 5", and section 5 is the section on APPLYING.  Read the fee as one on the application
-- (the head the draft priced), and the text as made prices the application and is silent on the receipt.
-- src:fees:27 | {{ח:תת|(ג)}} בעד קבלת רישיון או חידושו לפי {{ח:חיצוני|חוק הסדרת העיסוק בעבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר#סעיף 5|סעיף 5 לחוק}}, ישלם מבקש הרישיון אגרה בסכום של 284 שקלים חדשים {{ח:הערה|(מתואם לשנת 2025)}}.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 2(c) (src:fees:27)
GIVEN service IS A `Service under the Fees Regulations`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Fee stated in a vintage`
`the Fees Regulations as made state, reading regulation 2(c) as a fee on the application under section 5, for the service` service MEANS
    CONSIDER service
    WHEN `the service of filing an application for a licence or its renewal`
        THEN JUST `as made, regulation 2(c) — the fee for receiving a licence or renewing it`
    WHEN `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE `the Fees Regulations as made state, for the service` service

§§ `Regulation 3: update of fees`

-- (a) The amounts of the fees in regulation 2 are updated on each 1 January (the "update day") by the rate of
-- change of the new index against the base index, rounded to the nearest whole new shekel.  "New index": the
-- index published in the November before the update day.  "Base index": the index published in the November
-- before the PREVIOUS update day; for the first update day after the commencement day, the index published in
-- the month before the commencement.  "Index": the consumer price index the Central Bureau of Statistics publishes.
--
-- The update day is a recurring calendar date (kind R) and "the month before" is counted backwards in calendar
-- months (kind B): IL s.10 speaks of neither, so no IL s.10 function is called here.  Month arithmetic is done on
-- year and month NUMBERS, never on a date.
--
-- The index readings are an INPUT: the sources give none, and the Director General's notice under (b) is not in
-- them either.  "Published in a month" is read off the `published on` day of a reading, so that the reading
-- published in November is whichever reading carries a publication day in November.

-- src:fees:31 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} סכומי האגרות המפורטים {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 2|בתקנה 2}} יעודכנו ב־1 בינואר של כל שנה (להלן – יום העדכון) לפי שיעור השינוי של המדד החדש לעומת המדד היסודי, ויעוגל לשקל החדש השלם הקרוב; לעניין זה –
-- src:fees:32 | {{ח:תת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”המדד החדש“ – המדד שפורסם בחודש נובמבר שקדם ליום העדכון;
-- src:fees:33 | {{ח:תת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”המדד היסודי“ – המדד שפורסם בחודש נובמבר שקדם ליום העדכון הקודם, ולעניין יום העדכון הראשון שלאחר יום תחילתן של תקנות אלה – המדד שפורסם בחודש שלפני תחילתן של תקנות אלה;
-- src:fees:34 | {{ח:תת|סוג=הגדרה}} ”מדד“ – מדד המחירים לצרכן שמפרסמת הלשכה המרכזית לסטטיסטיקה.
-- Paraphrase (mine; the Hebrew governs): (a) the amounts of the fees specified in regulation 2 are updated on
-- 1 January of each year (the update day) by the rate of change of the new index against the base index, and rounded
-- to the nearest whole new shekel; for this purpose: "the new index" is the index published in the month of November
-- before the update day; "the base index" is the index published in the month of November before the previous update
-- day, and for the first update day after the commencement day of these regulations, the index published in the month
-- before their commencement; "index" is the consumer price index published by the Central Bureau of Statistics.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a) (src:fees:31-34)
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`regulation 3(a) — the update day of the year` y MEANS
    YMD y 1 1

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a) "the first update day after the commencement day" (src:fees:33)
GIVEN commencement IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`regulation 3(a) — the first update day after the commencement day` commencement MEANS
    `regulation 3(a) — the update day of the year` (DATE_YEAR commencement PLUS 1)

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a) "the first update day after the commencement day" (src:fees:33)
GIVEN commencement IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 3(a) — the year of the first update day after the commencement day` commencement MEANS
    DATE_YEAR (`regulation 3(a) — the first update day after the commencement day` commencement)

-- The calendar month before the month of a day, on year and month numbers.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a) "the month before their commencement" (src:fees:33)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Calendar month under regulation 3`
`regulation 3(a) — the calendar month before the month of` d MEANS
    IF   DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 1
    THEN `Calendar month under regulation 3` WITH `year of the calendar month` IS DATE_YEAR d MINUS 1
                             , `number of the calendar month` IS 12
    ELSE `Calendar month under regulation 3` WITH `year of the calendar month` IS DATE_YEAR d
                             , `number of the calendar month` IS DATE_MONTH d MINUS 1

-- "The index published in the month": the readings whose publication day falls in that calendar month.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a) "the index published in the month" (src:fees:32-34)
GIVEN month IS A `Calendar month under regulation 3`
      readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Price index reading`
`regulation 3(a) — the readings published in` month `, among` readings MEANS
    filter `was published in the month` readings
    WHERE
        `was published in the month` r MEANS
                DATE_YEAR (r's `published on`) EQUALS month's `year of the calendar month`
            AND DATE_MONTH (r's `published on`) EQUALS month's `number of the calendar month`

-- The other reading of the first base index: the index RELATING to the month (the June index, published in July).
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a) "the month before their commencement" (src:fees:33)
GIVEN month IS A `Calendar month under regulation 3`
      readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Price index reading`
`regulation 3(a) — the readings relating to` month `, among` readings MEANS
    filter `relates to the month` readings
    WHERE
        `relates to the month` r MEANS
                r's `year of the index` EQUALS month's `year of the calendar month`
            AND r's `month of the index` EQUALS month's `number of the calendar month`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 3(a) needs the index of a month, and no reading for that month was supplied` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 3(a) needs the index of a month, and no reading for that month was supplied"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 3(a) speaks of the index of a month, and two or more readings for that month were supplied` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 3(a) speaks of the index of a month, and two or more readings for that month were supplied"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 3(a) divides by the base index, and the base index supplied is not a positive number` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 3(a) divides by the base index, and the base index supplied is not a positive number"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 3(a) updates a stated fee from the day it took effect, and the stated fee has no such day` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 3(a) updates a stated fee from the day it took effect, and the stated fee has no such day"

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a) "the index" (src:fees:32-34)
GIVEN found IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 3(a) — the value of the one reading in` found MEANS
    CONSIDER found
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `regulation 3(a) needs the index of a month, and no reading for that month was supplied`
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY EMPTY THEN r's `value of the index`
    OTHERWISE `regulation 3(a) speaks of the index of a month, and two or more readings for that month were supplied`

-- "The new index": the index published in the November before the update day of the year y.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a) "the new index" (src:fees:32)
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 3(a) — the new index of the update day of the year` y `, among` readings MEANS
    `regulation 3(a) — the value of the one reading in`
        (`regulation 3(a) — the readings published in`
            (`Calendar month under regulation 3` WITH `year of the calendar month` IS y MINUS 1, `number of the calendar month` IS 11)
            `, among` readings)

-- "The base index".  For the first update day after the commencement day: the index published in the month before
-- the commencement (or, on the other reading, relating to it).  For every later update day: the index published in
-- the November before the previous update day, that is, the November two years before y.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a) "the base index" (src:fees:33)
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      ctx IS AN `Inputs of regulation 3`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 3(a) — the base index of the update day of the year` y `, under` ctx MEANS
    IF   y EQUALS `regulation 3(a) — the year of the first update day after the commencement day` (ctx's `the regulations came into force on`)
    THEN CONSIDER ctx's `the reading of regulation 3`'s `the base index`
         WHEN `the index published in the month before the commencement` THEN `the index published in the month before the commencement`
         WHEN `the index relating to the month before the commencement` THEN `the index relating to the month before the commencement`
    ELSE `the index published in the November before the previous update day`
    WHERE
        readings MEANS ctx's `index readings`
        `the month before the commencement` MEANS
            `regulation 3(a) — the calendar month before the month of` (ctx's `the regulations came into force on`)
        `the index published in the month before the commencement` MEANS
            `regulation 3(a) — the value of the one reading in` (`regulation 3(a) — the readings published in` `the month before the commencement` `, among` readings)
        `the index relating to the month before the commencement` MEANS
            `regulation 3(a) — the value of the one reading in` (`regulation 3(a) — the readings relating to` `the month before the commencement` `, among` readings)
        `the November before the previous update day` MEANS
            `Calendar month under regulation 3` WITH `year of the calendar month` IS y MINUS 2, `number of the calendar month` IS 11
        `the index published in the November before the previous update day` MEANS
            `regulation 3(a) — the value of the one reading in` (`regulation 3(a) — the readings published in` `the November before the previous update day` `, among` readings)

-- "The rate of change of the new index against the base index": (new - base) / base.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a) (src:fees:31)
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      ctx IS AN `Inputs of regulation 3`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 3(a) — the rate of change on the update day of the year` y `, under` ctx MEANS
    IF   base AT MOST 0
    THEN `regulation 3(a) divides by the base index, and the base index supplied is not a positive number`
    ELSE (new MINUS base) DIVIDED BY base
    WHERE
        new MEANS `regulation 3(a) — the new index of the update day of the year` y `, among` (ctx's `index readings`)
        base MEANS `regulation 3(a) — the base index of the update day of the year` y `, under` ctx

-- "Rounded to the nearest whole new shekel": the text does not say where an exact half goes.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a) "rounded to the nearest whole new shekel" (src:fees:31)
GIVEN mode IS A `Rounding of a half shekel`
      x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 3(a) — rounded to the nearest whole new shekel, a half shekel being treated by` mode `, the number` x MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `a half shekel is rounded up` THEN FLOOR (x PLUS 0.5)
    WHEN `a half shekel is rounded to the even shekel` THEN ROUND x
    WHEN `a half shekel is rounded down` THEN CEILING (x MINUS 0.5)

-- The first update day that applies to a stated amount.  An amount that took effect after the regulations
-- commenced is not updated on an update day that came before it existed.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a) (src:fees:31)
GIVEN fee IS A `Fee stated in a vintage`
      ctx IS AN `Inputs of regulation 3`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 3(a) — the year of the first update day that applies to the stated fee` fee `, under` ctx MEANS
    CONSIDER ctx's `the reading of regulation 3`'s `a later amount`
    WHEN `the first 1 January after the regulations commenced` THEN
        `regulation 3(a) — the year of the first update day after the commencement day` (ctx's `the regulations came into force on`)
    WHEN `the first 1 January after the amount took effect` THEN
        CONSIDER fee's `the day the stated amount took effect`
        WHEN JUST effective THEN `regulation 3(a) — the year of the first update day after the commencement day` effective
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `regulation 3(a) updates a stated fee from the day it took effect, and the stated fee has no such day`

-- The amount after the updates: each update day from the first that applies to the amount, up to the year of the
-- day asked about, multiplies by one plus the rate of change.  Rounding is after every update day (each update
-- is a text that the Director General republishes under (b)) or once at the end.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(a) (src:fees:31-34)
GIVEN fee IS A `Fee stated in a vintage`
      day IS A DATE
      ctx IS AN `Inputs of regulation 3`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 3(a) — the amount of the stated fee` fee `on the day` day `after the updates, under` ctx MEANS
    CONSIDER ctx's `the reading of regulation 3`'s `the objection charge`
    WHEN `regulation 3 updates the objection charge as a fee` THEN `the updated amount`
    WHEN `regulation 3 leaves the objection charge as printed` THEN
        IF   fee's `an objection charge rather than a fee`
        THEN stated
        ELSE `the updated amount`
    WHERE
        `the updated amount` MEANS
            CONSIDER ctx's `the reading of regulation 3`'s `the rounding`
            WHEN `regulation 3 rounds after every update day` THEN `rounded through` (DATE_YEAR day)
            WHEN `regulation 3 rounds once, after the last update day` THEN `rounded` (`unrounded through` (DATE_YEAR day))
        stated MEANS fee's `the amount stated`
        first MEANS `regulation 3(a) — the year of the first update day that applies to the stated fee` fee `, under` ctx
        `rounded` x MEANS
            `regulation 3(a) — rounded to the nearest whole new shekel, a half shekel being treated by` (ctx's `the reading of regulation 3`'s `a half shekel`) `, the number` x
        `the update of the year` y MEANS
            `regulation 3(a) — the rate of change on the update day of the year` y `, under` ctx
        `unrounded through` y MEANS
            BRANCH IF y LESS THAN first
                       THEN stated
                   IF `regulation 3 — the update of the year` y `binds on` day `, under` ctx
                       THEN `unrounded through` (y MINUS 1) TIMES (1 PLUS `the update of the year` y)
                   OTHERWISE `unrounded through` (y MINUS 1)
        `rounded through` y MEANS
            BRANCH IF y LESS THAN first
                       THEN stated
                   IF `regulation 3 — the update of the year` y `binds on` day `, under` ctx
                       THEN `rounded` (`rounded through` (y MINUS 1) TIMES (1 PLUS `the update of the year` y))
                   OTHERWISE `rounded through` (y MINUS 1)

-- Does the update of the year y bind on the day?  Taken: from its update day, which is what (a) says ("shall be
-- updated on 1 January").  Alternative: from the day the Director General's notice under (b) for that update
-- was published; (b) says the Director General shall publish the changed text, and not that publication is
-- what makes the update bind.
-- src:fees:35 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} המנהל הכללי של משרד העבודה יפרסם בהודעה ברשומות את נוסח {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 2|תקנה 2}} כפי שהשתנתה עקב האמור בתקנת משנה (א).
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(b) (src:fees:35)
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      day IS A DATE
      ctx IS AN `Inputs of regulation 3`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 3 — the update of the year` y `binds on` day `, under` ctx MEANS
    CONSIDER ctx's `the reading of regulation 3`'s `an update`
    WHEN `an update binds from its update day` THEN
        day AT LEAST `regulation 3(a) — the update day of the year` y
    WHEN `an update binds from the day of the Director General's notice` THEN
            day AT LEAST `regulation 3(a) — the update day of the year` y
        AND any `announces this update by the day` (ctx's `notices of the Director General`)
    WHERE
        `announces this update by the day` n MEANS
                n's `year of the update day` EQUALS y
            AND n's `published in Reshumot on` AT MOST day

-- The reading of regulation 3 that the encoding takes, and one value for each alternative.
-- Taken: an exact half shekel is rounded up; rounding after every update day; the base index of the first update
-- day is the index PUBLISHED in the month before the commencement; an amount that took effect later is first
-- updated on the first 1 January after it took effect; an update binds from its update day.
GIVETH A `Reading of regulation 3`
`the reading of regulation 3 that the encoding takes` MEANS
    `Reading of regulation 3` WITH
        `a half shekel` IS `a half shekel is rounded up`
        `the rounding` IS `regulation 3 rounds after every update day`
        `the base index` IS `the index published in the month before the commencement`
        `a later amount` IS `the first 1 January after the amount took effect`
        `an update` IS `an update binds from its update day`
        `the objection charge` IS `regulation 3 updates the objection charge as a fee`

GIVETH A `Reading of regulation 3`
`the reading of regulation 3 that rounds a half shekel to the even shekel` MEANS
    `Reading of regulation 3` WITH
        `a half shekel` IS `a half shekel is rounded to the even shekel`
        `the rounding` IS `regulation 3 rounds after every update day`
        `the base index` IS `the index published in the month before the commencement`
        `a later amount` IS `the first 1 January after the amount took effect`
        `an update` IS `an update binds from its update day`
        `the objection charge` IS `regulation 3 updates the objection charge as a fee`

GIVETH A `Reading of regulation 3`
`the reading of regulation 3 that rounds a half shekel down` MEANS
    `Reading of regulation 3` WITH
        `a half shekel` IS `a half shekel is rounded down`
        `the rounding` IS `regulation 3 rounds after every update day`
        `the base index` IS `the index published in the month before the commencement`
        `a later amount` IS `the first 1 January after the amount took effect`
        `an update` IS `an update binds from its update day`
        `the objection charge` IS `regulation 3 updates the objection charge as a fee`

GIVETH A `Reading of regulation 3`
`the reading of regulation 3 that rounds once, after the last update day` MEANS
    `Reading of regulation 3` WITH
        `a half shekel` IS `a half shekel is rounded up`
        `the rounding` IS `regulation 3 rounds once, after the last update day`
        `the base index` IS `the index published in the month before the commencement`
        `a later amount` IS `the first 1 January after the amount took effect`
        `an update` IS `an update binds from its update day`
        `the objection charge` IS `regulation 3 updates the objection charge as a fee`

GIVETH A `Reading of regulation 3`
`the reading of regulation 3 that takes the index relating to the month before the commencement` MEANS
    `Reading of regulation 3` WITH
        `a half shekel` IS `a half shekel is rounded up`
        `the rounding` IS `regulation 3 rounds after every update day`
        `the base index` IS `the index relating to the month before the commencement`
        `a later amount` IS `the first 1 January after the amount took effect`
        `an update` IS `an update binds from its update day`
        `the objection charge` IS `regulation 3 updates the objection charge as a fee`

GIVETH A `Reading of regulation 3`
`the reading of regulation 3 that updates a later amount from the first update day of the regulations` MEANS
    `Reading of regulation 3` WITH
        `a half shekel` IS `a half shekel is rounded up`
        `the rounding` IS `regulation 3 rounds after every update day`
        `the base index` IS `the index published in the month before the commencement`
        `a later amount` IS `the first 1 January after the regulations commenced`
        `an update` IS `an update binds from its update day`
        `the objection charge` IS `regulation 3 updates the objection charge as a fee`

GIVETH A `Reading of regulation 3`
`the reading of regulation 3 that lets an update bind from the Director General's notice` MEANS
    `Reading of regulation 3` WITH
        `a half shekel` IS `a half shekel is rounded up`
        `the rounding` IS `regulation 3 rounds after every update day`
        `the base index` IS `the index published in the month before the commencement`
        `a later amount` IS `the first 1 January after the amount took effect`
        `an update` IS `an update binds from the day of the Director General's notice`
        `the objection charge` IS `regulation 3 updates the objection charge as a fee`

-- Alternative for the fork "is the objection charge one of the fees that regulation 3(a) updates": regulation 2(b)
-- says "an amount of NIS 40", where (a), (c) and (d) say "a fee of", and (a) updates "the amounts of the fees".
GIVETH A `Reading of regulation 3`
`the reading of regulation 3 that leaves the objection charge as printed` MEANS
    `Reading of regulation 3` WITH
        `a half shekel` IS `a half shekel is rounded up`
        `the rounding` IS `regulation 3 rounds after every update day`
        `the base index` IS `the index published in the month before the commencement`
        `a later amount` IS `the first 1 January after the amount took effect`
        `an update` IS `an update binds from its update day`
        `the objection charge` IS `regulation 3 leaves the objection charge as printed`

-- (b) The Director General of the Ministry of Labour publishes in Reshumot the text of regulation 2 as changed.
-- The text states no time for it, so the duty carries no WITHIN.
-- src:fees:35 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} המנהל הכללי של משרד העבודה יפרסם בהודעה ברשומות את נוסח {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 2|תקנה 2}} כפי שהשתנתה עקב האמור בתקנת משנה (א).
-- Paraphrase (mine): (b) the Director General of the Ministry of Labour shall publish in a notice in Reshumot
-- the text of regulation 2 as it changed because of sub-regulation (a).
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 3(b) (src:fees:35)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under the Fees Regulations`
`regulation 3(b) — the Director General publishes the text of regulation 2 as changed` MEANS
    PARTY `the Director General of the Ministry of Labour`
    MUST `publish in Reshumot the text of regulation 2 as changed by the update`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Director General of the Ministry of Labour`
         BECAUSE "regulation 3(b): the text of regulation 2 as changed by the update was not published in Reshumot"

§§ `Regulation 4: payment of the fee as a condition of the licence, the exams and the objection`

-- The bar applies to a service for which a fee was fixed under the regulations, and does not apply once the
-- fee is paid in full.  Where a vintage fixes no fee for the service, "a fee was fixed" is false, and the bar is
-- not engaged: that is the taken reading (the alternative refuses; see g8-fees.l4).
-- src:fees:38 | {{ח:ת}} הרשם לא ייתן רישיון שנקבעה בעדו אגרה לפי תקנות אלה ולא יחדשו, וכן האגף להכשרה מקצועית לא יאפשר ביצוע של הבחינות הנדרשות או הגשת השגה על בחינות, שנקבעה בעדן אגרה לפי תקנות אלה, אלא אם כן מבקש הרישיון או השירות כאמור שילם את האגרה במלואה לפי תקנות אלה.
-- Paraphrase (mine; the Hebrew governs): the Registrar shall not give a licence for which a fee was fixed
-- under these regulations and shall not renew it, and the Training Division shall not allow the performance of
-- the required exams, or the lodging of an objection to exams, for which a fee was fixed under these regulations,
-- unless the applicant for the licence or for the service has paid the fee in full under these regulations.
@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4 (src:fees:38)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts regulation 4 asks about`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`regulation 4 — the bar applies to the service` facts MEANS
        facts's `a fee was fixed under the regulations for it`
    AND NOT facts's `the payer paid the fee in full`

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4, first limb: "shall not give a licence" (src:fees:38)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts regulation 4 asks about`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under the Fees Regulations`
`regulation 4 — the Registrar and giving the licence` facts MEANS
    IF   `regulation 4 — the bar applies to the service` facts
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         SHANT `give a licence for which a fee was fixed`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Registrar`
              BECAUSE "regulation 4: the Registrar gave a licence for which a fee was fixed and the fee was not paid in full"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4, first limb: "and shall not renew it" (src:fees:38)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts regulation 4 asks about`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under the Fees Regulations`
`regulation 4 — the Registrar and renewing the licence` facts MEANS
    IF   `regulation 4 — the bar applies to the service` facts
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         SHANT `renew a licence for which a fee was fixed`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Registrar`
              BECAUSE "regulation 4: the Registrar renewed a licence for which a fee was fixed and the fee was not paid in full"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4, second limb: "the Training Division shall not allow the performance of the required exams" (src:fees:38)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts regulation 4 asks about`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under the Fees Regulations`
`regulation 4 — the Training Division and allowing the exam` facts MEANS
    IF   `regulation 4 — the bar applies to the service` facts
    THEN PARTY `the Training Division`
         SHANT `allow the performance of an exam for which a fee was fixed`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Training Division`
              BECAUSE "regulation 4: the Training Division allowed an exam for which a fee was fixed and the fee was not paid in full"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 4, second limb: "or the lodging of an objection to exams" (src:fees:38)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts regulation 4 asks about`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under the Fees Regulations`
`regulation 4 — the Training Division and allowing the objection` facts MEANS
    IF   `regulation 4 — the bar applies to the service` facts
    THEN PARTY `the Training Division`
         SHANT `allow the lodging of an objection for which a fee was fixed`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Training Division`
              BECAUSE "regulation 4: the Training Division allowed an objection to an exam for which a fee was fixed and the fee was not paid in full"
    ELSE FULFILLED
